From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: mt6797-spm-sleep: mask the GIC by default

With gic_mask set, a charger plug-in woke a 120 s mem suspend at the
plug (the SPM slept 23.8 s), a lid open woke it at 18.9 s, and CPU0
never left WFI before the program returned. Without it the plug was
missed until the timer. Interrupts worked after each resume.

Mask the GIC by default, as the vendor does; gic_mask=0 still gives the
old behaviour for comparison.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c
@@ -242,7 +242,7 @@ module_param(pmic_modes, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(pmic_modes, "Set the static PMIC sleep modes for each suspend");
 
-static bool gic_mask;
+static bool gic_mask = true;
 module_param(gic_mask, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(gic_mask, "Disable every SPI but the SPM's at the GIC while CPU0 waits");
 
 static inline u32 spm_rd(u32 off)
